This is a collection of YANIs by users of the #nethack IRC channel on
freenode.net. Please excuse any old ideas that may be present.

[2]: Nethack has sex and booze and demons and other things that would
earn it a Mature rating if it was sold in stores. Why doesn't it also
have tobacco? I would like a pipe and "pipe weed" (as per Middle Earth
legend). Smoking should have some benefit for wizards like making it
easier to read spellbooks or to regenerate PW. --rogza
[I was imagining smoking as a special type of resting.  I didn't
imagine one would smoke and melee monsters at the same time.  Perhaps,
"Your pipe goes out," if you attack something or even if you move at
all. -az]

[3]: there should be a #smoke extended command --AskHL

[4]: polymorph applied to pet should be permanent as it already is, but
the pet should keep its XP lvl. This would 1.prevent people abusing
polytraps to get pets way above what they could tame (by getting them
to step on it over and over) and 2.safeguard hardwork levelling up a
pet --Xarann

[5]: Red dancing shoes. Applying them three times teleports you to
Home1. --shel-

[6]: wielding fish corpses should "slap", not "bash" --Botje

[7]: Being polymorphed into a smaller or larger creature should adjust
the amount of time it takes to eat a food item. --Grunt
[Interesting.  Should your size also affect the size of your stomach
and your rate of nutrition consumption? -az]

[8]: Add a small time delay (usleep?) before moving the player,
depending on the player's speed. Normal or fast would be instantaneous,
while slow/burdened/stressed/etc would be noticeable, making the player
look and feel slower. --shel-

[9]: Throwing ?oAcid at water elementals should make the potion
explode, as #dipping it does. --Botje

[10]: Pancakes thrown upwards should stick to the ceiling. Just 'cause.
--shel-

[11]: #nethack suggests "Your health currently feels amplified!" for
shock resistance be replaced with a better pun, either "You feel
grounded!" (or my personnal suggestion, "You suddenly feel very
grounded!") --Xarann
[The problem here is that being grounded is the opposite of having
shock resistance.  How about, "You feel like you're conducting yourself
wisely." or "You suddenly feel like you've been unearthed!" -az]

[12]: You can start fires with a flintstone. --nornagon
[ you would need steel too, of course, and this would dull your sword.
What would you do with the fire?  Would you need to find a flintstone
before you could light candles or lamps? -az]
[13]: Theme music. --nornagon
[.mid, .mod, .mp3, what?  This would break portability in a big way,
